# Example agent env files for ONE import of ONE world. Nothing here is a secret until you fill it in,
# and the filled files must never be committed: ".env" and ".env.*" are git-ignored in this
# repository, and these are not the app's or the server's .env.
#
# "Import a world" in the app makes the world and shows four tokens once. The helper
# (.agents/skills/api-data-automation/scripts/agent_api.py) reads ONE token per env file, so make
# four files in .agents/automations/, one for each token the app showed:
#
#   .agents/automations/.env.full          the FULL token        (guide and rules, remnants, lore, plots)
#   .agents/automations/.env.characters    the CHARACTERS token  (kind: character)
#   .agents/automations/.env.accessories   the ACCESSORIES token (kinds: clothes, adornment, object)
#   .agents/automations/.env.settings      the SETTINGS token    (the kinds you chose, "place" by default)
#
# Each file has exactly these lines, with that worker's token and the same server:

API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8788
API_TOKEN=replace-with-this-workers-token
API_AUTH_HEADER=Authorization
API_AUTH_SCHEME=Bearer
API_TIMEOUT=30

# A worker runs the helper with its own file, and only its own:
#   AGENT_AUTOMATION_ENV=.agents/automations/.env.characters
#   python .agents/skills/api-data-automation/scripts/agent_api.py GET /api/agent/worlds/<world>/cards --query kind=character
#
# Not in these files, because the helper does not read them and they are not secrets: the world's
# name, the source folder, the working folder (outside any repository) and the Nirmata repository.
# Those go in the import prompt that "Import a world" generates (<SOURCE-FOLDER>, <WORKING-FOLDER>,
# <NIRMATA-REPO>).
#
# Tokens expire (7, 30 or 90 days, as chosen) and can be revoked at once with the world's
# "Agent access" button. Revoke all four when the import is done.
#
# On Windows in Git Bash, set MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1 first, or "/api/..." is turned into a file path
# before the helper sees it (PowerShell and cmd are not affected).
